+````markdown name=ops/docs/operator_checklist.md
+# Operator Checklist — Run Production Proofs & Promote to Level 4
+
+Preconditions
+- Ensure Tekton pipelines and tasks exist in `cicd` namespace (level4-master-validation and dependencies).
+- Ensure Ray cluster, Prometheus, Jaeger, and required services are available.
+- Ensure the cluster service account used by Tekton has AWS credentials (or IRSA) to upload to the evidence bucket.
+- Place cosign signer key at a secure location accessible by the signer (or a KMS-backed signer); scripts assume /secrets/cosign.key for local runs.
+
+Step 1 — Apply PipelineRun (preferred, in-cluster)
+1. Edit the PR YAML:
+   - ops/tekton/pipelineruns/production_proofs_pipelinerun_filled.yaml
+   - Replace `s3://REPLACE_WITH_YOUR_EVIDENCE_BUCKET` with your S3 bucket (example: s3://aegis-evidence-prod)
+
+2. Apply:
+   - kubectl apply -f ops/tekton/pipelineruns/production_proofs_pipelinerun_filled.yaml
+   - Monitor: kubectl -n cicd get pipelineruns -w
+
+Step 2 — Apply via helper script (local)
+1. Make executable and run:
+   - chmod +x ops/scripts/apply_production_proofs_pr.sh
+   - ./ops/scripts/apply_production_proofs_pr.sh --bucket s3://aegis-evidence-prod
+
+Step 3 — Or trigger using GitHub Actions (remote)
+1. Using gh CLI:
+   - chmod +x ops/ci/gh_dispatch_ghcli.sh
+   - ./ops/ci/gh_dispatch_ghcli.sh --repo your-org/your-repo --workflow "Run Production Proofs" --bucket s3://aegis-evidence-prod
+
+2. Using curl + GITHUB_TOKEN:
+   - export GITHUB_TOKEN=ghp_xxx
+   - chmod +x ops/ci/gh_dispatch_curl.sh
+   - ./ops/ci/gh_dispatch_curl.sh --repo your-org/your-repo --workflow run_production_proofs.yml --bucket s3://aegis-evidence-prod
+
+Step 4 — After run completes: Acceptance & Postmortem
+1. Fetch acceptance summary (the orchestrator uploads to production_proofs/summary-*.json):
+   - aws s3 ls s3://aegis-evidence-prod/production_proofs/
+   - aws s3 cp s3://aegis-evidence-prod/production_proofs/summary-<timestamp>.json /tmp/acceptance.json
+
+2. Inspect acceptance locally:
+   - cat /tmp/acceptance.json
+   - Or run: python3 ops/validation/acceptance_checker.py --evidence s3://aegis-evidence-prod --out /tmp/acceptance.json
+
+3. If acceptance failed:
+   - python3 ops/validation/postmortem_generator.py --acceptance /tmp/acceptance.json
+   - Triage items from the postmortem and create tickets for owners (ML-Platform, SRE, Security, FinOps).
+
+Step 5 — Re-run incremental tests as fixes are applied
+- For example:
+  - To re-run OTEL checks: python3 services/telemetry/otel_coverage_checker.py
+  - To re-run OPA harness: python3 services/decisioning/opa_harness_coverage.py
+  - To re-run remediation harness: python3 services/failure/remediation_test_harness.py
+
+Step 6 — Finalize evidence & sign
+1. Bundle & sign evidence:
+   - ./ops/scripts/cosign_sign_evidence_bundle.sh
+2. Prepare compliance package for Legal:
+   - EVIDENCE_BUCKET=s3://aegis-evidence-prod ./ops/ops/prepare_compliance_package.sh
+
+Step 7 — Controlled Gatekeeper promotion (after acceptance + security signoff)
+1. Use the controlled CI job:
+   - In GitHub Actions run `Level4 Full Validation & Controlled Promote` with `promote_gatekeeper: yes`.
+   - Or run: ./ops/security/promote_gatekeeper_enforce_controlled.sh (only after manual review)
+
+Notes & Troubleshooting
+- If PipelineRun fails early, inspect Tekton logs:
+  - kubectl -n cicd logs <task-pod> --follow
+- If S3 uploads fail, ensure service account credentials and network egress to S3.
+- For cosign signing failures, verify cosign key path and permissions.
+- For legal/regulatory exceptions, ensure OPA rules include `require_legal` and approvals flow is tested.
+
+End of checklist.
+````
